    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The smallest prime factor of 9 is 3.\n\\begin{align}\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil&= \\boxed{8}\\end{align} For any integer $k$, $\\lceil x \\rceil = x$ iff $k \\leq x < (k+1)$\n$$\\begin{cases} \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{3}{2} = k-1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{3^2}{4} = k \\\\ \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{(k+1)^2}{4} = k+1 \\end{cases}$$\nHence, $\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\rceil=\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\rceil=\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\rceil=8$.",
